{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"8b73145dfa4dc335b37567f5640b486c5e9f6b0fd1cc53ed50242c2e7d600549","occurred_at":"2026-11-14T10:47:01Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_verified":true,"failure_class":"evidence","mapped_intervals":[[91,95]],"mapped_path":"apps/crq-python/ops/unit-live-binding.py","quoted_text":"DEPENDENCY_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"(?P<directive>Wants|Requires|Requisite|BindsTo|PartOf|Conflicts|\"\n    r\"WantedBy|RequiredBy|Also|Upholds|OnFailure|OnSuccess|Triggers|\"\n    r\"TriggersBy|Unit)\\s*=\\s*(?P<value>.*)\")\nUNIT_SUFFIXES = {\".service\", \".timer\", \".path\"}","reason":"The regex includes `Unit=` for timer/path activation but omits socket `Service=`, and `UNIT_SUFFIXES` omits `.socket`. A co-installed `ingress.socket` with `[Socket] Service=crq-tick.service` is therefore not parsed as an activation edge, so discovery can report `supported=True` while a foreign activator remains outside the adapter's fence and restoration set. This is an existing discovery correctness gap, not a new protection requirement.","target":"1503bc658f57ac2bd2b03951ee3a4449645e164d"},"finding_id":"42841950cecaca688de179637617a60ae60a3c44af0e4f837f15569867989a2e","previous_event_id":null,"review_id":"71ab2e271a7c905e211adfb4f874fdf0c67e494d899214b009ad550c97d9a67c"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:42841950cecaca688de179637617a60ae60a3c44af0e4f837f15569867989a2e:c4e8e7a1cb8f273610e6f7ec1aa14686326736cc9cf0be56a1bb056aa5a94f47"}